#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid "&turtlelang; Programming Reference"
msgstr "Manual de referencia do programador de &turtlelang;"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the reference for &kturtle;'s &turtlelang;. In this chapter we first "
"briefly touch all the <link linkend=\"different-instructions\">different "
"instruction types</link>. Then the <link linkend=\"commands\">commands</"
"link> are explained one by one. Then <link linkend=\"containers"
"\">containers</link>, <link linkend=\"math\">math</link>, <link linkend="
"\"questions\">questions</link> and <link linkend=\"controlling-execution"
"\">execution controllers</link> are explained. At last you are shown how to "
"create you own commands with <link linkend=\"learn\">learn</link>."
msgstr ""
"Este é o manual de referencia do &turtlelang; de &kturtle;. Neste capítulo "
"primeiro descreberemos brevemente os diferentes <link linkend=\"different-"
"instructions\">tipos de instruccións</link>, e logo explicaranse os <link "
"linkend=\"commands\">comandos</link> un por un. Despois explícanse os <link "
"linkend=\"containers\">contedores</link>, as <link linkend=\"math"
"\">matemáticas</link>, as <link linkend=\"questions\">perguntas</link> e os "
"<link linkend=\"controlling-execution\">controladores da execución</link>. "
"Finalmente explícase como crear os seus proprios comandos mediante <link "
"linkend=\"learn\">define</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "Different Instruction Types"
msgstr "Os tipos de instrucións"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As in any language, &turtlelang; has different types of words and symbols. "
"Here the differences between the types are briefly explained."
msgstr ""
"Como en calquera linguaxe, &turtlelang; ten tipos diferentes de palabras e "
"símbolos. Aquí explícanse brevemente as diferenzas entre os tipos."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:12 programming-reference.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands"
msgstr "Comandos"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using commands you tell the turtle or &kturtle; to do something. Some "
"commands need input, some give output."
msgstr ""
"Empregando comandos dille ao sapoconcho de &kturtle; que faga algo. Algúns "
"comandos precisan dunha entrada, outros xeran unha saída."

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# forward is a command that needs input, in this case the number 100:\n"
"forward 100"
msgstr ""
"# avanza é un comando que precisa dunha entrada, neste caso o número 100:\n"
"avanza 100"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a detailed overview of all commands that &kturtle; supports go <link "
"linkend=\"commands\">here</link>."
msgstr ""
"Para coñecer máis detalles acerca de todos os comandos soportados por "
"&kturtle; vaia <link linkend=\"commands\">aquí</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numbers"
msgstr "Números"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most likely you already know quite a bit about numbers. The way numbers are "
"used in &kturtle; is not much different from spoken language, or math."
msgstr ""
"Posibelmente xa saiba bastante acerca dos números. A maneira de utilizar os "
"números en &kturtle; non é moi diferente da oral, nen da matemática."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We have the so called natural numbers: <userinput>0</userinput>, "
"<userinput>1</userinput>, <userinput>2</userinput>, <userinput>3</"
"userinput>, <userinput>4</userinput>, <userinput>5</userinput>, etc. The "
"negative numbers: <userinput>-1</userinput>, <userinput>-2</userinput>, "
"<userinput>-3</userinput>, etc. And the numbers with decimals, or dot-"
"numbers, for example: <userinput>0.1</userinput>, <userinput>3.14</"
"userinput>, <userinput>33.3333</userinput>, <userinput>-5.05</userinput>, "
"<userinput>-1.0</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Temos os números naturais: <userinput>0</userinput>, <userinput>1</"
"userinput>, <userinput>2</userinput>, <userinput>3</userinput>, "
"<userinput>4</userinput>, <userinput>5</userinput> etc, os números "
"negativos: <userinput>-1</userinput>, <userinput>-2</userinput>, <userinput>-"
"3</userinput> etc. E tamén temos números con parte decimal, por exemplo: "
"<userinput>0.1</userinput>, <userinput>3.14</userinput>, <userinput>33.3333</"
"userinput>, <userinput>-5.05</userinput>, <userinput>-1.0</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Numbers can be used in <link linkend=\"math\">mathematical calculations</"
"link> and <link linkend=\"questions\">questions</link>. They can also be put "
"in <link linkend=\"containers\">containers</link>."
msgstr ""
"Os números poden ser utilizados en <link linkend=\"math\">cálculos "
"matemáticos</link> e <link linkend=\"questions\">perguntas</link>. Tamén "
"poden porse en <link linkend=\"containers\">contedores</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Numbers are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with dark red in the <link "
"linkend=\"the-code-editor\">code editor</link>."
msgstr ""
"Os números aparecen <glossterm>realzados</glossterm> en vermello escuro no "
"<link linkend=\"the-code-editor\">editor do código</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strings"
msgstr "Textos"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First an example: <screen>\n"
"print \"Hello, I'm a string.\"\n"
"</screen> In this example <userinput>print</userinput> is a command where "
"<userinput>\"Hello, I'm a string.\"</userinput> is a string. Strings start "
"and end with the <userinput>\"</userinput> mark, by these marks &kturtle; "
"knows it is a string."
msgstr ""
"Primeiro un exemplo: <screen>\n"
"escrebe \"Olá, son un texto.\"</screen>\n"
"Neste exemplo <userinput>escrebe</userinput> é un comando no que <userinput>"
"\"Olá, son un texto.\"</userinput> é un texto. Os textos comezan e rematan "
"con aspas, <userinput>\"</userinput>, mediante as cais &kturtle; sabe que é "
"un texto."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Strings can be put in <link linkend=\"containers\">containers</link>. Yet "
"they cannot be used in <link linkend=\"math\">mathematical calculations</"
"link> and <link linkend=\"questions\">questions</link>."
msgstr ""
"Os textos poden porse en <link linkend=\"containers\">contedores</link>. "
"Aínda así non poden ser empregados en <link linkend=\"math\">cálculos "
"matemáticos</link> ou <link linkend=\"questions\">perguntas</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Strings are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with red in the <link linkend="
"\"the-code-editor\">code editor</link>."
msgstr ""
"Os textos son <glossterm>realzados</glossterm> en vermello no <link linkend="
"\"the-code-editor\">editor do código</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "Names"
msgstr "Nomes"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When using the &turtlelang; programming language you create new things. If "
"you write a program you will often need <link linkend=\"containers"
"\">containers</link> and in some cases you need <link linkend=\"learn"
"\">learn</link> to create new commands. When making a new command with <link "
"linkend=\"learn\">learn</link> you will have to specify a name."
msgstr ""
"Cando empregue a linguaxe de programación &turtlelang; pode crear novos "
"textos. Se escrebe un programa a miúdo precisará <link linkend=\"containers"
"\">contedores</link> e nalgúns casos <link linkend=\"learn\">define</link> "
"para crear novos comandos. Cando faga un novo comando con <link linkend="
"\"learn\">define</link> terá que especificar un nome."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose any name, as long as it does not already have a meaning. For "
"instance you cannot name a function <link linkend=\"forward\">forward</"
"link>, since that name is already used for an internal command. <screen>\n"
"# here forward is used as a new command, \n"
"# but it already has a meaning so \n"
"# this will produce an error:\n"
"learn forward {\n"
"  print \"this is invalid\"\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"# this works:\n"
"learn myforward {\n"
"  print \"this is ok\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Names can contain only letters, numbers and underscores (_). Yet "
"they have to start with a letter. Container names have to start with the "
"container prefix ($)."
msgstr ""
"Pode escoller calquera nome mentres non teña xa asinado un significado. Por "
"exemplo non pode crear unha función chamada <link linkend=\"forward"
"\">avanza</link>, porque este nome xa é empregado por un comando interno. "
"<screen>\n"
"# aquí emprégase avanza como un comando novo,\n"
"# pero xa ten un significado, polo que \n"
"# dará un erro:\n"
"define avanza {\n"
"  escrebe \"isto non é válido\"\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"# isto funciona:\n"
"define adianta {\n"
"  escrebe \"isto serve\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Os nomes só poden conter letras, número e trazos baixos (_), e "
"teñen que comezar por unha letra. Os nomes de contedor teñen que comezar co "
"prefixo de contedor ($)."

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# here forward is used as a container, \n"
"# starting with the $ prefix, so it does\n"
"# not conflict with the forward command\n"
"$forward = 20\n"
"print $forward"
msgstr ""
"# aquí emprégase avanza como un contedor,\n"
"# polo que se prefixa cun $, polo que non\n"
"# entra en conflito co comando avanza\n"
"$avanza = 20\n"
"escrebe $avanza"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Containers are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with bolded purple in the "
"<link linkend=\"the-code-editor\">code editor</link>."
msgstr ""
"Os contedores <glossterm>reálzanse</glossterm> en letra grosa púrpura no "
"<link linkend=\"the-code-editor\">editor do código</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please read the documentation on <link linkend=\"containers\">containers</"
"link> and the <link linkend=\"learn\">learn</link> command for a better "
"explanation and more examples."
msgstr ""
"Lea a documentación acerca dos <link linkend=\"containers\">contedores</"
"link> e do comando <link linkend=\"learn\">define</link> para ter mellores "
"explicacións e máis exemplos."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "Assignments"
msgstr "Asinacións"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Assignment are done with the <userinput>=</userinput> symbol. In programming "
"languages it is better to read the single <userinput>=</userinput> not as "
"'equals' but as 'becomes'. The word 'equals' is more appropriate for the "
"<userinput>==</userinput> which is a <link linkend=\"questions\">question</"
"link>."
msgstr ""
"As asinacións fanse mediante o símbolo <userinput>=</userinput>. Nas "
"linguaxes de programación é mellor ler o <userinput>=</userinput> non como "
"\"é igual a\" senón como \"faise\". A expresión \"é igual a\" é máis "
"apropriada para o <userinput>==</userinput> que é unha <link linkend="
"\"questions\">pergunta</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Assignments are generally use for two reasons, (1) to add content <link "
"linkend=\"containers\">containers</link>, and (2) to modify the content of a "
"container. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Polo xeral as asinacións empréganse por dous motivos, (1) para engadir "
"contido aos <link linkend=\"containers\">contedores</link>, e (2) para "
"modificar o contido dun contedor. Por exemplo:"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$x = 10\n"
"# the container x now contains the number 10\n"
"$W = \"My age is: \"\n"
"# the container W now contains the string \"My age is: \"\n"
"# this prints the content of the containers 'W' and 'x' on the canvas\n"
"print $W + $x"
msgstr ""
"$x = 10\n"
"# o contedor x agora contén o número 10\n"
"$W = \"A miña idade é: \"\n"
"# o contedor W agora contén o texto \"A miña idade é: \"\n"
"# isto que segue escrebe o contido dos contedores \"W\" e \"x\"\n"
"escrebe $W + $x"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more examples see the section that explains <link linkend=\"containers"
"\">containers</link>."
msgstr ""
"Para máis exemplos consulte a sección que explica os <link linkend="
"\"containers\">contedores</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Math Symbols"
msgstr "Símbolos matemáticos"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kturtle; supports all basic math symbols: add (<userinput>+</userinput>), "
"subtract (<userinput>-</userinput>), multiply (<userinput>*</userinput>), "
"divide (<userinput>/</userinput>) and the brackets <userinput>(</userinput> "
"and <userinput>)</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"&kturtle; admite os símbolos matemáticos básicos: suma (<userinput>+</"
"userinput>), resta (<userinput>-</userinput>), multiplicación (<userinput>*</"
"userinput>), división (<userinput>/</userinput>) e os parénteses <userinput>"
"(</userinput> e <userinput>)</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a complete explanation and more examples see the <link linkend=\"math"
"\">math</link> section."
msgstr ""
"Para recibir unha explicación completa e máis exemplos consulte a sección de "
"<link linkend=\"math\">matemáticas</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:70 programming-reference.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions"
msgstr "Perguntas"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We can ask simple questions on which the answer will be 'true' or 'false'."
msgstr ""
"Podemos facer perguntas simples nas que a resposta sexa \"certo\" ou \"falso"
"\"."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using questions is extensively explained in the <link linkend=\"questions"
"\">questions</link> section."
msgstr ""
"O uso das perguntas é explicado en detalle na sección de <link linkend="
"\"questions\">perguntas</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Question Glue-Words"
msgstr "Encadeamento de perguntas"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Questions can be glued together with so called 'question glue'. The glue "
"words are <userinput>and</userinput>, <userinput>or</userinput>, and a "
"special glue-word: <userinput>not</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"As perguntas poden combinarse mediante as palabras-chave <userinput>e</"
"userinput>, <userinput>ou</userinput> e unha palabra especial: "
"<userinput>non</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using question-glue is explained in the <link linkend=\"question-glue"
"\">Question Glue</link> section."
msgstr ""
"A utilización destas palabras-chave explícase na sección <link linkend="
"\"question-glue\">Combinación de perguntas</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Comentarios"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Comments are lines that start with a <userinput>#</userinput>. For example: "
"<screen>\n"
"# this is a comment!\n"
"print \"this is not a comment\"\n"
"# the previous line is not a comment, but the next line is:\n"
"# print \"this is not a comment\"\n"
"</screen> We can add comments to the code for ourselves or for someone else "
"to read. Comments are used for: (1) adding a small description to the "
"program, (2) explaining how a piece of code works if it is a bit cryptic, "
"and (3) to 'comment-out' lines of code that should be (temporarily) ignored "
"(see the last line of the example)."
msgstr ""
"Os comentarios son liñas que comezan cun <userinput>#</userinput>. Por "
"exemplo: <screen>\n"
"# isto é un comentario!\n"
"escrebe \"isto non é un comentario\"\n"
"# a liña previa non é un comentario, pero a seguinte si o é:\n"
"# escrebe \"isto non é un comentario\"\n"
"</screen> Podemos engadir comentarios no código para axudarnos a nós mesmos "
"ou a outras persoas a comprender o que fai. Os comentarios son utilizados "
"para: (1) engadir unha pequena descrición do programa, (2) explicar como "
"funciona un pedazo de código se é algo lioso, e (3) para \"comentar\" liñas "
"de código que deben ser ignoradas temporalmente (por exemplo a última liña "
"do exemplo anterior)."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Commented lines are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with light grey in "
"the <link linkend=\"the-code-editor\">code editor</link>."
msgstr ""
"As liñas comentadas son <glossterm>realzadas</glossterm> en gris claro no "
"<link linkend=\"the-code-editor\">editor do código</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using commands you tell the turtle or &kturtle; to do something. Some "
"commands need input, some give output. In this section we explain all the "
"commands that can be used in &kturtle;. Please note that all build in "
"commands we discuss here are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with blue in "
"the <link linkend=\"the-code-editor\">code editor</link>, this can help you "
"to distinguish them."
msgstr ""
"Mediante os comandos pode dicirlle ao sapoconcho ou a &kturtle; que faga "
"algo. Algúns comandos precisan de parámetros, outros xeran un resultado. "
"Nesta sección explicamos todos os comandos que poden ser empregados en "
"&kturtle;. Lembre que todos os comandos incorporados que se explican aquí "
"serán <glossterm>realzados</glossterm> en azul no <link linkend=\"the-code-"
"editor\">editor do código</link>, o que o axudará a distinguilos."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving the turtle"
msgstr "Mover o sapoconcho"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are several commands to move the turtle over the screen."
msgstr "Hai varios comandos que moven o sapoconcho pola pantalla."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>forward (fw)</term>"
msgstr "<term>avanza (av)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>forward (fw)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>avanza (av)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "forward X"
msgstr "avanza X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>forward</userinput> moves the turtle forward by the amount of X "
"pixels. When the pen is down the turtle will leave a trail. "
"<userinput>forward</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>fw</"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>avanza</userinput> move o sapoconcho cara diante X píxeles. Cando "
"o lápis está pousado deixará un rastro. <userinput>avanza</userinput> pode "
"abreviarse como <userinput>av</userinput>"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>backward (bw)</term>"
msgstr "<term>recua (re)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>backward (bw)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>recua (re)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "backward X"
msgstr "recua X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>backward</userinput> moves the turtle backward by the amount of X "
"pixels. When the pen is down the turtle will leave a trail. "
"<userinput>backward</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>bw</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>recua</userinput> move o sapoconcho cara atrás X píxeles. Se o "
"lápis está pousado deixará un rastro. <userinput>recua</userinput> pode ser "
"abreviado como <userinput>re</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>turnleft (tl)</term>"
msgstr "<term>xiraesquerda (xe)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>turnleft (tl)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>xiraesquerda (xe)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "turnleft X"
msgstr "xiraesquerda X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>turnleft</userinput> commands the turtle to turn an amount of X "
"degrees to the left. <userinput>turnleft</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>tl</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>xiraesquerda</userinput> ordénalle ao sapoconcho que xire X graus "
"á esquerda. <userinput>xiraesquerda</userinput> pode abreviarse como "
"<userinput>xe</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>turnright (tr)</term>"
msgstr "<term>xiradereita (xd)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>turnright (tr)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>xiradereita (xd)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "turnright X"
msgstr "xiradereita X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>turnright</userinput> the turtle to turn an amount of X degrees "
"to the right. <userinput>turnright</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>tr</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>xiradereita</userinput> ordénalle ao sapoconcho que xire X graus "
"á dereita. <userinput>xiradereita</userinput> pode abreviarse como "
"<userinput>xd</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>direction (dir)</term>"
msgstr "<term>direccion (dir)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>direction (dir)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>direccion (dir)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "direction X"
msgstr "direccion X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>direction</userinput> set the turtle's direction to an amount of "
"X degrees counting from zero, and thus is not relative to the turtle's "
"previous direction. <userinput>direction</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>dir</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>direccion</userinput> fai que o sapoconcho tome unha ruta a X "
"graus do cero, polo que non é relativa á anterior ruta que seguise o "
"sapoconcho. <userinput>direccion</userinput> pode abreviarse como "
"<userinput>dir</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>center</term>"
msgstr "<term>vaiaocentro</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>center</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>vaiaocentro</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>center</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>vaiaocentro</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>center</userinput> moves the turtle to the center on the canvas."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>vaiaocentro</userinput> leva o sapoconcho ao centro do lenzo."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>go</term>"
msgstr "<term>vai</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>go</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>vai</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "go X,Y"
msgstr "vai X,Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>go</userinput> commands the turtle to go to a certain place on "
"the canvas. This place is X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm> "
"from the left of the canvas, and Y <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</"
"glossterm> form the top of the canvas."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>vai</userinput> fai que o sapoconcho vaia a un lugar concreto do "
"lenzo. Este lugar está a X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">píxeles</glossterm> "
"do borde esquerdo do lenzo e a Y <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">píxeles</"
"glossterm> da parte de riba do lenzo."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>gox</term>"
msgstr "<term>vaix</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>gox</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>vaix</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "gox X"
msgstr "vaix X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gox</userinput> using this command the turtle will move to X "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm> from the left of the canvas "
"whilst staying at the same height."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>vaix</userinput> fai que o sapoconcho vaia a unha posición "
"situada a X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">píxeles</glossterm> do borde "
"esquerdo do lenzo sen desprazarse en altura."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>goy</term>"
msgstr "<term>vaiy</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>goy</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>vaiy</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "goy Y"
msgstr "vaiy Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gox</userinput> using this command the turtle will move to Y "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm> from the top of the canvas "
"whilst staying at the same distance from the left border of the canvas."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>vaiy</userinput> fai que o sapoconcho vaia a unha posición "
"situada a Y <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">píxeles</glossterm> do cume do "
"lenzo sen desprazarse en horizontal."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the commands <userinput>go</userinput>, <userinput>gox</userinput>, "
"<userinput>goy</userinput> and <userinput>center</userinput> the turtle will "
"not draw a line, no matter if the pen is up or down."
msgstr ""
"Cando se utilizan os comandos <userinput>vai</userinput>, <userinput>vaix</"
"userinput>, <userinput>vaiy</userinput> e <userinput>vaiaocentro</userinput> "
"o sapoconcho non debuxa a liña, con independencia de que o lápis estexa "
"erguido ou pousado."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where is the turtle?"
msgstr "Onde está o sapoconcho?"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two commands which return the position of the turtle on the screen."
msgstr "Hai dous comandos que din a posición do sapoconcho na pantalla."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>getx</term>"
msgstr "<term>coordenadaX</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>getx</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>coordenadaX</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>getx</userinput> returns the number of pixels from the left of "
"the canvas to the current position of the turtle."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>coordenadaX</userinput> devolve a cantidade de píxeles que hai "
"desde a esquerda do lenzo até a posición do sapoconcho."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>gety</term>"
msgstr "<term>coordenadaY</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>gety</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>coordenadaY</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gety</userinput> returns the number of pixels from the top of the "
"canvas to the current position of the turtle."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>coordenadaY</userinput> devolve a cantidade de píxeles que hai do "
"cume do lenzo até a posición do sapoconcho."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "The turtle has a pen"
msgstr "O sapoconcho ten un lápis"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The turtle has a pen that draws a line when the turtle moves. There are a "
"few commands to control the pen. In this section we explain these commands."
msgstr ""
"O sapoconcho ten un lápis que debuxa unha liña á medida que se move o "
"animal. Hai uns poucos comandos que controlan este lápis. Nesta sección "
"explicarémolos."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>penup (pu)</term>"
msgstr "<term>subelapis (sl)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>penup (pu)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>subelapis (sl)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "penup"
msgstr "subelapis"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>penup</userinput> lifts the pen from the canvas. When the pen is "
"<quote>up</quote> no line will be drawn when the turtle moves. See also "
"<userinput>pendown</userinput>. <userinput>penup</userinput> can be "
"abbreviated to <userinput>pu</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>subelapis</userinput> separa o lápis do lenzo. Cando o lápis está "
"<quote>subido</quote> non se debuxan liñas ao moverse o sapoconcho. Consulte "
"tamén <userinput>baixalapis</userinput>. <userinput>subeLapis</userinput> "
"pode abreviarse como <userinput>sl</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>pendown (pd)</term>"
msgstr "<term>baixalapis (bl)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>pendown (pd)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>baixalapis (bl)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "pendown"
msgstr "baixalapis"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>pendown</userinput> presses the pen down on the canvas. When the "
"pen is press <quote>down</quote> on the canvas a line will be drawn when the "
"turtle moves. See also <userinput>penup</userinput>. <userinput>pendown</"
"userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>pd</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>baixalapis</userinput> pousa o lápis no lenzo. Cando o lápis está "
"<quote>baixado</quote> debúxanse liñas cando se move o sapoconcho. Consulte "
"tamén <userinput>subelapis</userinput>. <userinput>baixalapis</userinput> "
"pode abreviarse como <userinput>bl</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>penwidth (pw)</term>"
msgstr "<term>ancholapis (al)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>penwidth (pw)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>ancholapis (al)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "penwidth X"
msgstr "ancholapis X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>penwidth</userinput> sets the width of the pen (the line width) "
"to an amount of X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>. "
"<userinput>penwidth</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>pw</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ancholapis</userinput> estabelece o grosor do trazo co valor de X "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">píxeles</glossterm>. <userinput>ancholapis</"
"userinput> pode abreviarse como <userinput>al</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>pencolor (pc)</term>"
msgstr "<term>corlapis (cl)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>pencolor (pc)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>corlapis (cl)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "pencolor R,G,B"
msgstr "corlapis R,G,B"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>pencolor</userinput> sets the color of the pen. "
"<userinput>pencolor</userinput> takes an <glossterm linkend=\"rgb\">RGB "
"combination</glossterm> as input. <userinput>pencolor</userinput> can be "
"abbreviated to <userinput>pc</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>corlapis</userinput> estabelece a cor do trazo. "
"<userinput>corlapis</userinput> toma como parámetro unha <glossterm linkend="
"\"rgb\">combinación RGB</glossterm>. <userinput>corlapis</userinput> code "
"abreviarse como <userinput>cl</userinput>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands to control the canvas"
msgstr "Comandos para controlar o lenzo"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are several commands to control the canvas."
msgstr "Hai varios comandos que controlan o lenzo."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>canvassize (cs)</term>"
msgstr "<term>tamañolenzo (tlz)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>canvassize (cs)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>tamañolenzo (tlz)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "canvassize X,Y"
msgstr "tamañolenzo X,Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the <userinput>canvassize</userinput> command you can set the size of "
"the canvas. It takes X and Y as input, where X is the new canvas width in "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>, and Y is the new height of "
"the canvas in <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>. "
"<userinput>canvassize</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>cs</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Mediante o comando <userinput>tamañolenzo</userinput> pode axustar o tamaño "
"da área. Toma X e Y como entradas, onde X é o novo ancho do lenzo en "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">píxeles</glossterm> e Y é o novo alto en "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">píxeles</glossterm>. <userinput>tamañolenzo</"
"userinput> pode abreviarse como <userinput>tlz</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>canvascolor (cc)</term>"
msgstr "<term>corlenzo (clz)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>canvascolor (cc)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>corlenzo (clz)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "canvascolor R,G,B"
msgstr "corlenzo R,G,B"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>canvascolor</userinput> set the color of the canvas. "
"<userinput>canvascolor</userinput> takes an <glossterm linkend=\"rgb\">RGB "
"combination</glossterm> as input. <userinput>canvascolor</userinput> can be "
"abbreviated to <userinput>cc</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>corlenzo</userinput> estabelece a cor do lenzo. "
"<userinput>corlenzo</userinput> toma unha <glossterm linkend=\"rgb"
"\">combinación RGB</glossterm> como entrada. <userinput>corlenzo</userinput> "
"pode abreviarse como <userinput>clz</userinput>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands to clean up"
msgstr "Comandos para borrar"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two commands to clean up the canvas after you have made a mess."
msgstr "Hai dous comandos para limpar o lenzo cando o emborrona."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>clear (ccl)</term>"
msgstr "<term>borra (br)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>clear (ccl)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>borra (br)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "clear"
msgstr "borra"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With <userinput>clear</userinput> you can clean all drawings from the "
"canvas. All other things remain: the position and angle of the turtle, the "
"canvascolor, the visibility of the turtle, and the canvas size."
msgstr ""
"Con <userinput>borra</userinput> pode borrar do lenzo todos os debuxos. As "
"demais cousas fican: a posición e ángulo do sapoconcho, a cor do lenzo, a "
"visibilidade do sapoconcho e o tamaño do lenzo."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>reset</term>"
msgstr "<term>reinicia</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>reset</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>reinicia</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>reset</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>reinicia</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>reset</userinput> cleans much more thoroughly than the "
"<userinput>clear</userinput> command. After a <userinput>reset</userinput> "
"command everything is like is was when you had just started &kturtle;. The "
"turtle is positioned at the middle of the screen, the canvas color is white, "
"the turtle draws a black line on the canvas and the canvassize is set to 400 "
"x 400 pixels."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>reinicia</userinput> limpa máis a fondo do que o fai o comando "
"<userinput>borra</userinput>. Despois de executar un comando "
"<userinput>reinicia</userinput> todo volta a ser como cando iniciou "
"&kturtle;. O sapoconcho estará posto no centro da pantalla, a cor do lenzo "
"será branco, debuxarase cun trazo negro e o tamaño do lenzo será de 400 x "
"400 píxeles."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "The turtle is a sprite"
msgstr "O sapoconcho é un sprite"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First a brief explanation of what sprites are: sprites are small pictures "
"that can be moved around the screen, like we often see in computer games. "
"Our turtle is also a sprite. For more info see the glossary on <glossterm "
"linkend=\"sprites\">sprites</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"Os sprites son pequenas imaxes que se poden mover pola pantalla, como se ve "
"nos xogos de consola. O noso animaliño tamén é un sprite. Para saber máis "
"acerca disto, consulte a entrada <glossterm linkend=\"sprites\">sprites</"
"glossterm> no glosario."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next you will find a full overview on all commands to work with sprites."
msgstr ""
"A seguir ten un resumo completo de todos os comandos que traballan sobre "
"sprites."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[The current version of &kturtle; does not yet support the use of sprites "
"other than the turtle. With future versions you will be able to change the "
"turtle into something of your own design]"
msgstr ""
"[A versión actual de &kturtle; aínda non permite utilizar outros sprites que "
"non sexan o sapoconcho. En versións futuras poderá mudar para outro deseño á "
"súa escolla]"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>spriteshow (ss)</term>"
msgstr "<term>mostrasapoconcho (msc)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>spriteshow (ss)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>mostrasapoconcho (msc)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "spriteshow"
msgstr "mostrasapoconcho"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>spriteshow</userinput> makes the turtle visible again after it "
"has been hidden. <userinput>spriteshow</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>ss</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mostrasapoconcho</userinput> fai de novo visíbel ao sapoconcho se "
"antes foi agochado. <userinput>mostrasapoconcho</userinput> pode abreviarse "
"como <userinput>msc</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>spritehide (sh)</term>"
msgstr "<term>agochasapoconcho (asc)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>spritehide (sh)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>agochasapoconcho (asc)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "spritehide"
msgstr "agochasapoconcho"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>spritehide</userinput> hides the turtle. This can be used if the "
"turtle does not fit in your drawing. <userinput>spritehide</userinput> can "
"be abbreviated to <userinput>sh</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>agochasapoconcho</userinput> fai invisíbel ao sapoconcho. Isto "
"pode empregarse se o animal non couber no debuxo. "
"<userinput>agochasapoconcho</userinput> pode abreviarse como <userinput>asc</"
"userinput>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can the turtle write?"
msgstr "Pode escreber o sapoconcho?"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The answer is: <quote>yes</quote>. The turtle can write: it writes just "
"about everything you command it to."
msgstr ""
"A resposta é: <quote>pode</quote>. A tartaruga pode escreber, e escreberá "
"calquera cousa que lle mande."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>print</term>"
msgstr "<term>escrebe</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>print</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>escrebe</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "print X"
msgstr "escrebe X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>print</userinput> command is used to command the turtle to "
"write something on the canvas. <userinput>print</userinput> takes numbers "
"and strings as input. You can <userinput>print</userinput> various numbers "
"and strings using the <quote>+</quote> symbol. See here a small example:"
msgstr ""
"O comando <userinput>escrebe</userinput> ordénalle ao sapoconcho que escreba "
"algo no lenzo. <userinput>escrebe</userinput> pode tomar textos e números "
"como parámetros. Pode <userinput>escrebe</userinput>r varios números e "
"cadeas mediante o símbolo <quote>+</quote>. Aquí vai un exemplo:"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$year = 2003\n"
"$author = \"Cies\"\n"
"print $author + \" started the KTurtle project in \" + $year + \" and still "
"enjoys working on it!\""
msgstr ""
"$ano = 2009\n"
"$autor = \"Bruno\"\n"
"escrebe $autor + \" debuxou unha nora en KTurtle no ano\" + $ano + \" e "
"gustoulle moito!\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>fontsize</term>"
msgstr "<term>letratamaño</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>fontsize</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>letratamaño</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "fontsize X"
msgstr "letratamaño X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>fontsize</userinput> sets the size of the font that is used by "
"<userinput>print</userinput>. <userinput>fontsize</userinput> takes one "
"input which should be a number. The size is set in <glossterm linkend="
"\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>letratamaño</userinput> modifica o tamaño de letra utilizado ao "
"<userinput>escreber</userinput>. <userinput>letratamaño</userinput> toma un "
"argumento numérico. O tamaño indícase en <glossterm linkend=\"pixels"
"\">píxeles</glossterm>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "A command that rolls dice for you"
msgstr "Un comando que escolle ao chou"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is one command that rolls dice for you, it is called "
"<userinput>random</userinput>, and it is very useful for some unexpected "
"results."
msgstr ""
"Hai un comando que saca un número ao chou, chámase <userinput>aleatorio</"
"userinput> e é moi útil para ter resultados inesperados."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>random (rnd)</term>"
msgstr "<term>aleatorio (alea)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>random (rnd)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>aleatorio (alea)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "random X,Y"
msgstr "aleatorio X,Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>random</userinput> is a command that takes input and gives "
"output. As input are required two numbers, the first (X) sets the minimum "
"output, the second (Y) sets the maximum. The output is a randomly chosen "
"number that is equal or greater than the minimum and equal or smaller than "
"the maximum. Here a small example: <screen>\n"
"repeat 500 {\n"
"  $x = random 1,20\n"
"  forward $x\n"
"  turnleft 10 - $x\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Using the <userinput>random</userinput> command you can add a bit "
"of chaos to your program."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>aleatorio</userinput> é un comando que toma unha entrada e saca "
"un resultado. Como entrada precisa de dous números, o primeiro (X) é o "
"resultado mínimo, o segundo (Y) o máximo. A saída é un número escollido ao "
"chou que é como mínimo o menor e como máximo o maior. Aquí vai un exemplo:"
"<screen>\n"
"repite 500 {\n"
"  $x = aleatorio 1,20\n"
"  avanza $x\n"
"  xiraesquerda 10 - $x\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Mediante o comando <userinput>aleatorio</userinput> pode "
"introducir algo de caos no programa."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input and feedback though dialogs"
msgstr "Introdución de datos e obtención de resultados mediante diálogos"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A dialog is a small pop-up window that provides some feedback or asks for "
"some input. &kturtle; has two commands for dialogs, namely: "
"<userinput>message</userinput> and <userinput>ask</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"Un diálogo é unha pequena fiestra emerxente que lle dá algo de información "
"ou que lle pide algún dato. &kturtle; ten dous comandos para diálogos, que "
"son: <userinput>mostra</userinput> e <userinput>pergunta</userinput>"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>message</term>"
msgstr "<term>mostra</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>message</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>mostra</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "message X"
msgstr "mostra X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>message</userinput> command takes a <link linkend=\"string"
"\">string</link> as input. It shows a pop-up dialog containing the text from "
"the <link linkend=\"string\">string</link>."
msgstr ""
"O comando <userinput>mostra</userinput> toma un <link linkend=\"string"
"\">texto</link> como entrada, e mostra un diálogo que contén o <link linkend="
"\"string\">texto</link>."

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"message \"Cies started the KTurtle project in 2003 and still enjoys working "
"on it!\""
msgstr ""
"mostra \"Bruno debuxou unha nora en KTurtle no ano 2008 e gustoulle moito!\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>ask</term>"
msgstr "<term>pergunta</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>ask</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>pergunta</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "ask X"
msgstr "pergunta X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>ask</userinput> takes a <link linkend=\"string\">string</link> as "
"input. It shows a pop-up dialog containing the text from the string, just "
"like the <link linkend=\"message\">message</link>. But in addition to it "
"also puts an input field on the dialog. Through this input filed the user "
"can enter a <link linkend=\"number\">number</link> or a <link linkend="
"\"string\">string</link> which can be stored in a <link linkend=\"containers"
"\">container</link>. For example <screen>\n"
"$in = ask \"What is you age?\"\n"
"$out = 2003 - $in\n"
"print \"In 2003 you where \" + $out + \" years old at some point.\"\n"
"</screen> When a user cancels the input dialog, or does not enter anything "
"at all the <link linkend=\"containers\">container</link> is emptied."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>pergunta</userinput> toma un <link linkend=\"string\">texto</"
"link> como entrada. Mostra un diálogo que contén o texto, como fai <link "
"linkend=\"message\">mostra</link>, pero ademais tamén pon un campo de texto "
"no diálogo. Mediante este campo o usuario pode introducir un <link linkend="
"\"number\">número</link> ou un <link linkend=\"string\">texto</link> que "
"pode gardar nun <link linkend=\"containers\">contedor</link>. Por exemplo "
"<screen>\n"
"$idade = pergunta \"Cantos anos tes?\"\n"
"$resultado = 2003 - $idade\n"
"escrebe \"En 2003 tiñas \" + $resultado + \" anos.\"</screen>\n"
"Cando un usuario cancela o diálogo de pergunta, ou non insere nada, o <link "
"linkend=\"containers\">contedor</link> será baleirado."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Containers"
msgstr "Contedores"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Containers are letters or words that can be used by the programmer to store "
"a number or a text. Containers that contain a number are called <link "
"linkend=\"variables\">variables</link>, containers that can contain text are "
"called <link linkend=\"string\">string</link>. Containers can be identified "
"by the container character <quote>$</quote> that precedes their usage."
msgstr ""
"Os contedores son letras ou palabras que poden ser utilizadas polo "
"programador para gardar un número ou texto. Aos contedores que conteñen un "
"número chámaselles  <link linkend=\"variables\">variábeis</link>, e aos que "
"conteñen letras <link linkend=\"string\">textos</link>. Os contedores "
"identifícanse facilmente polo caracter <quote>$</quote> que levan diante do "
"nome."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Containers that are not used contain nothing. An example: <screen>\n"
"print $N\n"
"</screen> This will print nothing and you get an error message."
msgstr ""
"Os contedores que non están a ser utilizados non conteñen nada. Exemplo: "
"<screen>\n"
"escrebe $N\n"
"</screen> Non escreberá nada e pola contra mostrará unha mensaxe de erro."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "Variables: number containers"
msgstr "Variábeis: contedores de números"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let us start with an example: <screen>\n"
"$x = 3\n"
"print $x\n"
"</screen> In the first line the letter <userinput>x</userinput> is made into "
"a variable (number container). As you see the value of the variable "
"<userinput>x</userinput> is set to 3. On the second line the value is "
"printed."
msgstr ""
"Comecemos cun exemplo: <screen>\n"
"$x = 3\n"
"escrebe $x\n"
"</screen> Na primeira liña a letra <userinput>x</userinput> é convertida "
"nunha variábel (contedor de números). Como pode ver, a variábel "
"<userinput>x</userinput> toma o valor 3. Na segunda liña escrébese no lenzo "
"o valor."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that if we wanted to print an <quote>x</quote> that we should have "
"written"
msgstr ""
"Lembre que se quixese escreber un <quote>x</quote> deberíamos ter feito"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid "print \"x\""
msgstr "escrebe \"x\""

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"That was easy, now a bit harder example: <screen>\n"
"$A = 2004\n"
"$B = 25\n"
"$C = $A + $B\n"
"\n"
"# the next command prints \"2029\"\n"
"print $C\n"
"backward 30\n"
"# the next command prints \"2004 plus 25\"\n"
"print $A + \" plus \" + $B\n"
"backward 30\n"
"# the next command prints \"1979\"\n"
"print $A - $B\n"
"</screen> In the first two lines the variables <userinput>A</userinput> and "
"<userinput>B</userinput> are set to 2004 and 25. On the third line the "
"variable <userinput>C</userinput> is set to <userinput>A + B</userinput>, "
"which is 2029. The rest of the example consists of 3 <userinput>print</"
"userinput> commands with <userinput>backward 30</userinput> in between. The "
"<userinput>backward 30</userinput> is there to make sure every output is on "
"a new line. In this example you also see that variables can be used in <link "
"linkend=\"math\">mathematical calculations</link>."
msgstr ""
"Iso foi sinxelo, agora fagámolo algo máis complicado: <screen>\n"
"$A = 2004\n"
"$B = 25\n"
"$C = $A + $B\n"
"\n"
"# o seguinte comando escrebe \"2029\"\n"
"escrebe $C\n"
"recua 30\n"
"# o seguinte comando escrebe \"2004 máis 25\"\n"
"escrebe $A + \" máis \" + $B\n"
"recua 30\n"
"# o seguinte comando escrebe \"1979\"\n"
"escrebe $A - $B\n"
"</screen> Nas primeiras dúas liñas dáselles os valores 2004 e 25 ás "
"variábeis <userinput>A</userinput> e <userinput>B</userinput>. Na terceira "
"liña a variábel <userinput>C</userinput> toma o valor <userinput>A + B</"
"userinput>, que é 2029. O resto do exemplo consiste en 3 comandos "
"<userinput>escrebe</userinput> con <userinput>recua 30</userinput> polo "
"medio. Estes <userinput>recua</userinput> foron postos ahí para garantir que "
"cada cousa fose escrita nunha liña nova. Neste exemplo tamén vemos como as "
"variábeis poden ser empregadas en <link linkend=\"math\">cálculos "
"matemáticos</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "Containers that contain text (strings)"
msgstr "Contedores que conteñen letras (textos)"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In programming code the regular text is usually started and ended with "
"quotes. As we have already seen: <screen>\n"
"print \"Hello programmer!\"\n"
"</screen> The regular is delimited with quotes. These pieces of regular text "
"we call <link linkend=\"strings\">strings</link>."
msgstr ""
"No código de programación os textos polo xeral comézanse e termínanse con "
"aspas. Como xa vimos: <screen>\n"
"escrebe \"Olá programador!\"\n"
"</screen> Estas pezas de texto ordinario son chamadas <link linkend=\"strings"
"\">textos</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Strings can also be stored in <link linkend=\"containers\">containers</link> "
"just like <link linkend=\"number\">numbers</link> Strings are a lot like "
"variables. The biggest difference is that they contain text in stead of "
"numbers. For this reason strings cannot be used in <link linkend=\"math"
"\">mathematical calculations</link> and <link linkend=\"questions"
"\">questions</link>. An example of the use of strings: <screen>\n"
"$x = \"Hello \"\n"
"$name = ask \"Please enter your name...\"\n"
"print $x + $name + \", how are you?\"\n"
"</screen> On the first line the string <userinput>x</userinput> is set to "
"<quote>Hello </quote>. On the second line the string <userinput>name</"
"userinput> is set to the output of the <userinput>ask</userinput> command. "
"On the third line the program prints a composition of three strings on the "
"canvas."
msgstr ""
"Os textos tamén son gardados en <link linkend=\"containers\">contedores</"
"link> como os <link linkend=\"number\">números</link>, e teñen moitos "
"parecidos coas variábeis. A maior diferenza é que conteñen texto no canto de "
"números. Por este motivo non poden ser utilizados en <link linkend=\"math"
"\">cálculos matemáticos</link> nen <link linkend=\"questions\">perguntas</"
"link>. Vexamos un exemplo de utilización de textos: <screen>\n"
"$saudo = \"Olá \"\n"
"$nome = pergunta \"Dime como te chamas...\"\n"
"escrebe $x + $nome + \", como estás?\"\n"
"</screen> Na primeira liña o texto <userinput>x</userinput> toma o valor de "
"<quote>Olá </quote>. Na segunda o texto <userinput>nome</userinput> toma o "
"valor do resultado de <userinput>perguntar</userinput>. Na terceira liña o "
"programa escrebe no lenzo unha composición de tres textos."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This program ask you to enter your name. When you, for instance, enter the "
"name <quote>Paul</quote>, the program prints <quote>Hello Paul, how are you?"
"</quote>. Please note that the plus (+) is the only math symbol that you can "
"use with strings."
msgstr ""
"Este programa pídelle que introduza o seu nome. Se escrebe, por exemplo, o "
"nome <quote>Paulo</quote>, o programa escrebe <quote>Olá Paulo, como estás?</"
"quote>. Lembre que o signo máis (+) é o único símbolo matemático que pode "
"utilizar cos textos."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can the Turtle do math?"
msgstr "Sabe matemáticas o sapoconcho?"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes, &kturtle; will do your math. You can add (+), subtract (-), multiply "
"(*), and divide (/). Here is an example in which we use all of them: "
"<screen>\n"
"$a = 20 - 5\n"
"$b = 15 * 2\n"
"$c = 30 / 30\n"
"$d = 1 + 1\n"
"print \"a: \"+$a+\", b: \"+$b+\", c: \"+$c+\", d: \"+$d \n"
"</screen> Do you know what value a, b, c and d have? Please note the use of "
"the <link linkend=\"assignment\">assignment</link> symbol <userinput>=</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Si, &kturtle; sabe matemáticas. Pode sumar (+), restar (-), multiplicar (*), "
"e dividir (/). Aquí vai un exemplo no que se utilizan estas operacións:"
"<screen>\n"
"$a = 20 - 5\n"
"$b = 15 * 2\n"
"$c = 30 / 30\n"
"$d = 1 + 1\n"
"escrebe \"a: \" + $a + \", b: \" + $b + \", c: \" + $c + \" e d: \" + $d\n"
"</screen> Sabe os valores que teñen a, b e c?. Poña atención a que se "
"emprega o símbolo de <link linkend=\"assignment\">asinación</link>, "
"<userinput>=</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you just want a simple calculation to be done you can do something like "
"this:"
msgstr "Se só quer facer un cálculo simples pode facer algo como isto:"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid "print 2004-12"
msgstr "escrebe 2004-12"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now an example with parentheses: <screen>\n"
"print ( ( 20 - 5 ) * 2 / 30 ) + 1\n"
"</screen> The expressions inside parentheses will be calculated first. In "
"this example, 20-5 will be calculated, then multiplied by 2, divided by 30, "
"and then 1 is added (giving 2)."
msgstr ""
"Agora un exemplo con parénteses: <screen>\n"
"escrebe ((20 -5) * 2 / 30 ) + 1\n"
"</screen> As expresións entre parénteses serán calculadas primeiro. Neste "
"exemplo, calcularase 20-5, logo multiplicarase por 2, dividirase entre 30, e "
"finalmente engádeselle 1, co que dá o resultado 2."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kturtle; has advanced mathematical features. It knows the number "
"<userinput>pi</userinput> and trigonometrical functions like <userinput>sin</"
"userinput>, <userinput>cos</userinput>, <userinput>tan</userinput>, "
"<userinput>arcsin</userinput>, <userinput>arccos</userinput>, "
"<userinput>arctan</userinput> and the functions <userinput>sqrt</userinput> "
"and <userinput>exp</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"&kturtle; ten capacidades matemáticas avanzadas. Sabe o número "
"<userinput>pi</userinput>, e funcións trigonométricas como <userinput>seno</"
"userinput>, <userinput>coseno</userinput>, <userinput>tanxente</userinput>, "
"<userinput>arcoseno</userinput>, <userinput>arcocoseno</userinput>, "
"<userinput>arcotanxente</userinput> e as funcións <userinput>raiz</"
"userinput> e <userinput>exp</userinput>."

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>pi</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>pi</primary>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "sin, cos, tan"
msgstr "seno, coseno, tanxente"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid "arcsin, arccos, arctan"
msgstr "arcoseno, arcocoseno, arcotanxente"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "sqrt, exp"
msgstr "raiz, exp"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid "Let the turtle round your numbers"
msgstr "Deixe que o sapoconcho redondee os números"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you need integers in calculations, use this function."
msgstr "Se precisa de números enteiros nos cálculos, empregue esta función."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>round</term>"
msgstr "<term>redondea</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>round</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>redondea</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "round(x)"
msgstr "redondea (x)"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>round</userinput> the given number to the nearest integer. "
"<screen>\n"
"print round(10.8)\n"
"forward 20\n"
"print round(10.3)\n"
"forward 20\n"
"</screen> With this code the turtle will print the numbers 11 and 10."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>redondea</userinput> o número indicado ao enteiro máis próximo. "
"<screen>\n"
"escrebe redondea(10.8)\n"
"avanza 20\n"
"escrebe redondea(10.3)\n"
"avanza 20\n"
"</screen> Con este código o sapoconcho escreberá os números 11 e 10."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid "Asking questions, getting answers..."
msgstr "Facer perguntas, obter respostas..."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>if</userinput></link> and <link linkend="
"\"while\"><userinput>while</userinput></link> are <link linkend="
"\"controlling-execution\">execution controllers</link> that we will discuss "
"in the next section. In this section we use the <link linkend=\"if"
"\"><userinput>if</userinput></link> command to explain questions."
msgstr ""
"<link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>se</userinput></link> e <link linkend=\"while"
"\"><userinput>mentres</userinput></link> son <link linkend=\"controlling-"
"execution\">controladores da execución</link> que explicaremos na seguinte "
"sección. Nesta utilizaremos o comando <link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>se</"
"userinput></link> para explicar as perguntas."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A simple example of a question: <screen>\n"
"$x = 6\n"
"if $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> In this example the question is the <userinput>x &gt; 5</"
"userinput> part. If the answer to this question is 'true' the code between "
"the brackets will be executed. Questions are an important part of "
"programming and often used together with <link linkend=\"controlling-"
"execution\">execution controllers</link>, like <link linkend=\"if"
"\"><userinput>if</userinput></link>. All numbers and <link linkend="
"\"variables\">variables</link> (number containers) can be compared to each "
"other with questions."
msgstr ""
"Un exemplo simples de pergunta: <screen>\n"
"$x = 6\n"
"se $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  escrebe \"olá\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Neste exemplo a pergunta é <userinput>x &gt; 5</userinput>. Se a "
"resposta e isto é \"certo\" executarase o código entre as chaves. As "
"perguntas son unha parte importantísima da programación e a miúdo son "
"empregadas xunto con <link linkend=\"controlling-execution\">controladores "
"de execución</link>, como <link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>se</userinput></"
"link>. Todos os número e <link linkend=\"variables\">variábeis</link> "
"(contedores de números) poden ser comparados uns cos outros en perguntas."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here are all possible questions:"
msgstr "Estas son todas as posíbeis perguntas:"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid "Types of questions"
msgstr "Tipos de perguntas"

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "a == b"
msgstr "a == b"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "equals"
msgstr "é igual a"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>a</userinput> equals "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> se <userinput>a</userinput> é igual a "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid "a != b"
msgstr "a != b"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "not-equals"
msgstr "é diferente de"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>a</userinput> does not equal "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> se <userinput>a</userinput> non é igual a "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid "a &gt; b"
msgstr "a &gt; b"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid "greater than"
msgstr "maior que"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>a</userinput> is greater than "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> se <userinput>a</userinput> é maior que "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "a &lt; b"
msgstr "a &lt; b"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid "smaller than"
msgstr "menor que"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>a</userinput> is smaller than "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> se <userinput>a</userinput> é menor que "
"<userinput>b</userinput>"

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "a &gt;= b"
msgstr "a &gt;= b"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "greater than or equals"
msgstr "maior ou igual que"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>a</userinput> is greater than or "
"equals <userinput>b</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> se <userinput>a</userinput> é maior ou "
"igual a <userinput>b</userinput>"

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "a &lt;= b"
msgstr "a &lt;= b"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid "smaller than or equals"
msgstr "menor ou igual que"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>a</userinput> is smaller than or "
"equals <userinput>b</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> se <userinput>a</userinput> é menor ou "
"igual a <userinput>b</userinput>"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid "Question Glue"
msgstr "Encadeamento de perguntas"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Question glue-words enable us to glue questions into one big question. "
"<screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"if ($a &lt; $b) and ($b == 5) {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> In this example the glue-word <userinput>and</userinput> is used "
"to glue 2 questions (<userinput>a &lt; 5</userinput>, <userinput>b == 5</"
"userinput>) together. If one side of the <userinput>and</userinput> would "
"answer <quote>false</quote> the whole question would answer <quote>false</"
"quote>, because with the glue-word <userinput>and</userinput> both sides "
"need to be <quote>true</quote> in order to answer <quote>true</quote>. "
"Please do not forget to use the brackets around the questions!"
msgstr ""
"As palabras de encadeamento de perguntas permítennos xuntar varias perguntas "
"nunha máis elaborada. <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"se ($a &lt; $b) e ($b == 5) {\n"
"  escrebe \"Olá\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Neste exemplo a palabra combinadora <userinput>e</userinput> é "
"empregada para xuntar 2 perguntas (<userinput>a &lt; 5</userinput>, "
"<userinput>b == 5</userinput>) nunha. Se un lado do <userinput>e</userinput> "
"é <quote>falso</quote> toda a resposta será <quote>falso</quote>, porque con "
"<userinput>e</userinput> ambos os dous lados deben ser <quote>certo</quote> "
"para que a resposta sexa <quote>certo</quote>. Por favor non se esqueza de "
"empregar os parénteses arredor das perguntas!"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is a schematic overview; a more detailed explanation follows below:"
msgstr ""
"Este é un resumo esquemático, a seguir exponse unha explicación detallada:"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid "Question glue-words"
msgstr "Palabras de encadeamento de perguntas"

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>and</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>e</userinput>"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid "Both sides need to be 'true' in order to answer 'true'"
msgstr ""
"Ambos os dous lados deben ser \"certo\" para que a resposta sexa \"certo\""

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>or</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>ou</userinput>"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid "If one of the sides is 'true' the answer is 'true'"
msgstr "Se un dos lados é \"certo\" a resposta será \"certo\""

#. Tag: userinput
#: programming-reference.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>not</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>non</userinput>"

#. Tag: entry
#: programming-reference.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Special case: only works on one question! Changes 'true' into 'false' and "
"'false' into 'true'."
msgstr ""
"Caso especial: só opera sobre unha pergunta! Muda o estado de \"certo\" para "
"\"falso\" ou de \"falso\" para \"certo\""

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:536
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>and</title>"
msgstr "<title>e</title>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>and</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>e</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When two questions are glued together with <userinput>and</userinput>, both "
"sides of the <userinput>and</userinput> have to be 'true' in order to result "
"in 'true'. An example: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"if (($a &lt; 10) and ($b == 5)) and ($a &lt; $b) {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> In this example you see a glued question glued onto an other "
"question."
msgstr ""
"Cando dúas perguntas son xuntadas mediante un <userinput>e</userinput>, "
"ambos os dous lados do <userinput>e</userinput> deben ser \"certo\" para que "
"o resultado sexa \"certo\". Por exemplo: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"se (($a &lt; 10) e ($b == 5)) e ($a &lt; $b) {\n"
"  escrebe \"Olá\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Neste exemplo vese unha pergunta combinada dentro de outra "
"pergunta combinada."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>or</title>"
msgstr "<title>ou</title>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>or</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>ou</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If one of the two questions that are glued together with <userinput>or</"
"userinput> is 'true' the result will be 'true'. An example: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"if (($a &lt; 10) or ($b == 10)) or ($a == 0) {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> In this example you see a glued question glued onto an other "
"question."
msgstr ""
"Se unha das dúas perguntas que están a ser combinadas con <userinput>ou </"
"userinput> é \"certo\" o resultado será \"certo\". Por exemplo: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"se (($a &lt; 10) ou ($b == 10)) ou ($a == 0) {\n"
" escrebe \"Olá\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Neste exemplo vese unha pergunta combinada dentro de outra "
"pergunta combinada."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>not</title>"
msgstr "<title>non</title>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>not</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>non</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>not</userinput> is a special question glue-word because it only "
"works for one question at the time. <userinput>not</userinput> changes "
"'true' into 'false' and 'false' into 'true'. An example: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"if not (($a &lt; 10) and ($b == 5)) {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"}\n"
"else\n"
"{\n"
"  print \"not hello ;-)\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> In this example the glued question is 'true' yet the "
"<userinput>not</userinput> changes it to 'false'. So in the end <userinput>"
"\"not hello ;-)\"</userinput> is printed on the <link linkend=\"the-canvas"
"\">canvas</link>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>non</userinput> é unha palabra combinadora especial porque só "
"opera sobre unha pergunta á vez. <userinput>non</userinput> troca o estado "
"de \"certo\" para \"falso\" ou viceversa. Por exemplo: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"se non (($a &lt; 10) e ($b == 5)) {\n"
"  escrebe \"Olá\"\n"
"}\n"
"noutrocaso\n"
"{\n"
"  escrebe \"Adeus\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Neste exemplo a pergunta combinada é \"certo\", pero o "
"<userinput>non</userinput> troca o resultado para \"falso\". Deste xeito, "
"escrébese <userinput>\"Adeus\"</userinput> no <link linkend=\"the-canvas"
"\">lenzo</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling execution"
msgstr "Control da execución"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The execution controllers enable you &mdash; as their name implies &mdash; "
"to control execution."
msgstr ""
"Os controladores da execución permítenlle, como indica o nome, controlar o "
"fluxo de execución."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Execution controlling commands are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with "
"dark green in a bold font type. The brackets are mostly used together with "
"execution controllers and they are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with "
"bolded black."
msgstr ""
"Os comandos de control da execución son <glossterm>realzados</glossterm> en "
"letra verde grosa. As chaves utilízanse caseque sempre xunto cos "
"controladores de execución e son <glossterm>realzados</glossterm> en letra "
"negra grosa."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid "Have the turtle wait"
msgstr "Facer que o sapoconcho agarde"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:570
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have done some programming in &kturtle; you have might noticed that "
"the turtle can be very quick at drawing. This command makes the turtle wait "
"for a given amount of time."
msgstr ""
"Se programou algo en &kturtle; xa se terá decatado de que o sapoconcho pode "
"ser moi moi moi rápido cando debuxa. Este comando fai que agarde durante un "
"tempo."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>wait</term>"
msgstr "<term>agarda</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>wait</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>agarda</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid "wait X"
msgstr "agarda X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>wait</userinput> makes the turtle wait for X seconds. <screen>\n"
"repeat 36 {\n"
"  forward 5\n"
"  turnright 10\n"
"  wait 0.5\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> This code draws a circle, but the turtle will wait half a second "
"after each step. This gives the impression of a slow-moving turtle."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>agarda</userinput> fai que o sapoconcho estexa quedo durante X "
"segundos. <screen>\n"
"repite 36 {\n"
"  avanza 5\n"
"  xiradereita 10\n"
"  agarda 0.5\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Este código debuxa un círculo, pero o animal agardará medio "
"segundo tras cada paso. Isto dá a impresión dun sapoconcho lento."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid "Execute \"if\""
msgstr "Executar \"se\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>if</term>"
msgstr "<term>se</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>if</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>se</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid "if <link linkend=\"questions\">question</link> { ... }"
msgstr "se <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The code that is placed between the brackets will only be executed "
"<userinput>if</userinput> the answer to the <link linkend=\"questions"
"\">question</link> is <quote>true</quote>. Please read for more information "
"on <link linkend=\"questions\">questions</link> in the <link linkend="
"\"questions\">question section</link>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 6\n"
"if $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  print \"x is greater than five!\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> On the first line <userinput>x</userinput> is set to 6. On the "
"second line the <link linkend=\"questions\">question</link> <userinput>x "
"&gt; 5</userinput> is asked. Since the answer to this question is "
"<quote>true</quote> the execution controller <userinput>if</userinput> will "
"allow the code between the brackets to be executed"
msgstr ""
"O código que vai entre as chaves só será executado <userinput>se</userinput> "
"a resposta á <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> é <quote>certo</"
"quote>. Achará máis información acerca das <link linkend=\"questions"
"\">perguntas</link> nas <link linkend=\"questions\">sección de perguntas</"
"link>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 6\n"
"se $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  escrebe \"x é maior que cinco!\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Na primeira liña <userinput>x</userinput> toma o valor 6. Na "
"segunda liña faise a <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> "
"<userinput>x &gt; 5</userinput>. Xa que a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> o "
"controlador de execución <userinput>se</userinput> permitirá que se execute "
"o código entre as chaves"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid "If not, in other words: \"else\""
msgstr "Se non, o caso contrario: \"noutrocaso\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>else</term>"
msgstr "<term>noutrocaso</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>else</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>noutrocaso</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "if question { ... } else { ... }"
msgstr "se pergunta { ... } noutrocaso { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>else</userinput> can be used in addition to the execution "
"controller <link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>if</userinput></link>. The code "
"between the brackets after <userinput>else</userinput> is only executed if "
"the answer to the <link linkend=\"questions\">question</link> that is asked "
"is <quote>false</quote>. <screen>\n"
"reset\n"
"$x = 4\n"
"if $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  print \"x is greater than five!\"\n"
"}\n"
"else\n"
"{\n"
"  print \"x is smaller than six!\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> The <link linkend=\"questions\">question</link> asks if "
"<userinput>x</userinput> is greater than 5. Since <userinput>x</userinput> "
"is set to 4 on the first line the answer to the question is <quote>false</"
"quote>. This means the code between the brackets after <userinput>else</"
"userinput> gets executed."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>noutrocaso</userinput> pode empregarse xunto co controlador de "
"execución <link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>se</userinput></link>. O código "
"entre as chaves que seguen a <userinput>noutrocaso</userinput> só será "
"executado se a resposta á <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> é "
"<quote>falso</quote>. <screen>\n"
"reinicia\n"
"$x = 4\n"
"se non 5 &gt; $x {\n"
" escrebe \"x é maior que cinco!\"\n"
"}\n"
"noutrocaso\n"
"{\n"
"  escrebe \"x é menor que seis!\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> A <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> é se <userinput>x</"
"userinput> é maior que 5 (pero do revés ao levar a negación diante). Xa que "
"<userinput>x</userinput> vale 4 a resposta é <quote>falso</quote>. Isto "
"significa que se executará o código entre as chaves que seguen a "
"<userinput>noutrocaso</userinput>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"while\" loop"
msgstr "O ciclo \"mentres\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>while</term>"
msgstr "<term>mentres</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>while</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>mentres</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid "while <link linkend=\"questions\">question</link> { ... }"
msgstr "mentres <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The execution controller <userinput>while</userinput> is a lot like <link "
"linkend=\"if\"><userinput>if</userinput></link>. The difference is that "
"<userinput>while</userinput> keeps repeating (looping) the code between the "
"brackets until the answer to the <link linkend=\"questions\">question</link> "
"is <quote>false</quote>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 1\n"
"while $x &lt; 5 {\n"
"  forward 10\n"
"  wait 1\n"
"  $x = $x + 1\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> On the first line <userinput>x</userinput> is set to 1. On the "
"second line the <link linkend=\"questions\">question</link> <userinput>x "
"&lt; 5</userinput> is asked. Since the answer to this question is "
"<quote>true</quote> the execution controller <userinput>while</userinput> "
"starts executing the code between the brackets until the answer to the <link "
"linkend=\"questions\">question</link> is <quote>false</quote>. In this case "
"the code between the brackets will be executed 4 times, because every time "
"the fifth line is executed <userinput>x</userinput> increases by 1."
msgstr ""
"O controlador de execución <userinput>mentres</userinput> seméllase moito a "
"<link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>se</userinput></link>. A diferenza é que "
"<userinput>mentres</userinput> repite o código entre as chaves até que a "
"resposta á <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> sexa <quote>falso</"
"quote>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 1\n"
"mentres $x &lt; 5 {\n"
"  avanza 10\n"
"  agarda 1\n"
"  $x = $x + 1\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Na primeira liña <userinput>x</userinput> toma o valor de 1. Na "
"segunda liña faise a <link linkend=\"questions\">pergunta</link> "
"<userinput>x &lt; 5</userinput>. Dado que a resposta é <quote>certo</quote> "
"o controlador de execución <userinput>mentres</userinput> comeza a executar "
"o código entre as chaves até que a resposta á <link linkend=\"questions"
"\">pergunta</link> sexa <quote>falso</quote>. Neste caso executarase 4 "
"veces, porque cada vez que se executa a quinta liña <userinput>x</userinput> "
"aumenta 1."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"repeat\" loop"
msgstr "O ciclo \"repite\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>repeat</term>"
msgstr "<term>repite</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>repeat</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>repite</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid "repeat number { ... }"
msgstr "repite número { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The execution controller <userinput>repeat</userinput> is a lot like <link "
"linkend=\"while\"><userinput>while</userinput></link>. The difference is "
"that <userinput>repeat</userinput> keeps repeating (looping) the code "
"between the brackets for the given number."
msgstr ""
"O controlador de execucion <userinput>repite</userinput> seméllase moito a "
"<link linkend=\"while\"><userinput>mentres</userinput></link>. A diferenza é "
"que <userinput>repite</userinput> executa o código entre as chaves o número "
"dado de veces."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"for\" loop, a counting loop"
msgstr "O ciclo \"desde\", un ciclo cun contador"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>for</term>"
msgstr "<term>desde</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>for</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>desde</primary>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid "step"
msgstr "pasando"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"for <userinput>start point</userinput> to <userinput>end point</userinput> "
"{ ... }"
msgstr ""
"desde <userinput>ponto inicial</userinput> ate <userinput>ponto final</"
"userinput> {...}"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>for</userinput> loop is a <quote>counting loop</quote>, &ie; "
"it keeps count for you. <screen>\n"
"for $x = 1 to 10 {\n"
"  print $x * 7\n"
"  forward 15\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Every time the code between the brackets is executed the "
"<userinput>x</userinput> is increased by 1, until <userinput>x</userinput> "
"reaches the value of 10. The code between the brackets prints the "
"<userinput>x</userinput> multiplied by 7. After this program finishes its "
"execution you will see the times table of 7 on the canvas."
msgstr ""
"O bucle <userinput>para</userinput> é un <quote>bucle con contador</quote>, "
"&ie;, mantén por si o reconto. <screen>\n"
"desde $x = 1 ate 10 {\n"
"  escrebe $x * 7\n"
"  avanza 15\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Cada vez que se executa o código entre as chaves o <userinput>x</"
"userinput> aumenta en 1, até que <userinput>x</userinput> acada o valor de "
"10. O código nas chaves escrebe o valor do <userinput>x</userinput> "
"multiplicado por 7. Cando este programa remate a execución verá a táboa de "
"multiplicar do 7 no lenzo."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
